{
  "publication_number": "CN114707670A",
  "title": "Non-label data-oriented heterogeneous federated learning method and system",
  "assignee": "National University of Defense Technology",
  "filing_date": "2022-04-07",
  "publication_date": "2022-07-05",
  "pse": {
    "problem": "Existing federated learning methods suffer from high communication overhead, data privacy risks, and are unable to effectively utilize system heterogeneity or handle unlabeled data.",
    "solution_function": "The invention proposes a heterogeneous federated learning method that addresses the above issues by locally training adaptive models on various client devices using unlabeled data. The system collectively trains a global model that incorporates diverse features of the client data while preserving user privacy and reducing communication overhead.",
    "solution_structure": "The system consists of multiple client devices with varying capabilities, a server, and a central management unit. Each client device has local processing units, memory for storing unlabeled data, and secure communication channels to exchange information with other clients and the server.",
    "solution_implementation": "The method involves three stages: (1) preprocessing, where the unlabeled data is preprocessed on the client side to extract features; (2) model training, where adaptive models are trained locally on each client device based on their computational resources and system environment; (3) global aggregation, where the trained models are securely shared with the server for model updates, resulting in a globally adapted model.",
    "effect": "The proposed method reduces communication overhead by minimizing data transmission, preserves user privacy through local training, effectively utilizes system heterogeneity by adapting models to various client devices, and handles unlabeled data without the need for extensive labeling efforts."
  },
